To further optimize the memory usage of the sieve array for very large inputs, we can use a segmented sieve algorithm. The segmented sieve is an extension of the Sieve of Eratosthenes that is used to find primes in a range of numbers. It is more memory-efficient for large ranges, as it only stores the numbers in the range and marks them as non-prime based on the primes found in the initial sieve.

